1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,257
给一条鱼做动画，最经典的办法是骨骼
The classic way to animate a fish is a skeleton:

2
00:00:04,257 --> 00:00:07,613
六十到一百个关节，想怎么动就怎么动
sixty to a hundred joints, and it can do anything you like.

3
00:00:08,373 --> 00:00:10,922
可《ABZÛ》要的，是这样的画面
But ABZÛ wanted something like this.

4
00:00:11,822 --> 00:00:17,122
你看角落这里，我想大概有一万一千条鱼
you can see in the corner there, I think it's about 11,000 fish or something.

5
00:00:17,222 --> 00:00:18,822
这些是巨大的鲹鱼
These are giant trevallies,

6
00:00:18,822 --> 00:00:25,022
它们同时在游，每一条的节奏都不一样
and they all are swimming with a unique timing of their swim cycle at the same time.

7
00:00:25,322 --> 00:00:28,222
我们试过用带骨骼的鱼来做这个场景
when we tried to do this scene with skeleton fish,

8
00:00:28,222 --> 00:00:32,622
屏幕上大概只能放 30 条鱼
we only could get like 30 fish on the screen.

9
00:00:32,622 --> 00:00:34,822
所以差别非常大
So it's a huge difference.

10
00:00:35,322 --> 00:00:37,455
三十条，到一万一千条
Thirty fish, versus eleven thousand.

11
00:00:37,455 --> 00:00:40,572
这一期，我们拆开《ABZÛ》的鱼
This episode, we take ABZÛ's fish apart.

12
00:00:42,872 --> 00:00:44,629
骨骼动画贵在哪？
Why are skeletons expensive?

13
00:00:44,629 --> 00:00:47,793
每一帧，每个关节都要算一次变换
Every frame, every joint needs its transform computed,

14
00:00:47,793 --> 00:00:50,780
再把每个顶点按权重蒙到骨头上
and every vertex is skinned to its bones by weight.

15
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:54,914
一万条鱼乘一百个关节，就是一百万个关节
Ten thousand fish times a hundred joints is a million joints,

16
00:00:54,914 --> 00:00:56,863
每秒还要再算六十遍
sixty times a second.

17
00:00:57,423 --> 00:00:59,270
所以他们干脆把骨骼拿掉了
So they took the skeletons away.

18
00:01:00,470 --> 00:01:02,787
所有鱼共用一个静态网格
Every fish shares one static mesh,

19
00:01:02,787 --> 00:01:05,434
用实例化一次画出成千上万份
drawn thousands of times in a single instanced call.

20
00:01:05,694 --> 00:01:07,912
这项技术原本多用来画草地
The technique is usually used for grass;

21
00:01:07,912 --> 00:01:09,982
每个实例只带一小份数据
each instance carries only a tiny bit of data.

22
00:01:10,242 --> 00:01:14,397
在这期的演示里，每条鱼只有三十二个字节
In this demo, each fish is just thirty-two bytes:

23
00:01:14,397 --> 00:01:17,041
位置、相位、速度和转向
position, phase, velocity and turn rate.

24
00:01:18,341 --> 00:01:20,485
没有骨骼，鱼怎么动？
Without bones, how does a fish move?

25
00:01:20,485 --> 00:01:23,165
答案是在材质里直接挪顶点
By moving its vertices right in the material.

26
00:01:23,725 --> 00:01:26,492
第一层，整条鱼左右平移
Layer one: the whole fish slides side to side.

27
00:01:26,492 --> 00:01:29,062
第二层，绕中心点偏航
Layer two: it yaws around its center.

28
00:01:29,822 --> 00:01:33,454
第三层，一道正弦波沿着脊椎传向尾巴
Layer three: a sine wave travels down the spine to the tail.

29
00:01:33,454 --> 00:01:35,996
第四层，身体沿脊椎扭转
Layer four: the body twists along the spine.

30
00:01:36,756 --> 00:01:40,033
再加一张蒙板，只让后半身摆动
Add a mask so only the back half swings,

31
00:01:40,033 --> 00:01:44,082
一条会游的鱼就出来了，一根骨头都没用
and you have a swimming fish without a single bone.

32
00:01:45,582 --> 00:01:48,294
四层动作都由同一个相位驱动
All four layers run off a single phase.

33
00:01:48,294 --> 00:01:52,023
每条鱼起始相位不同，鱼群就不会整齐划一
Give every fish its own starting phase, and the school stops marching in lockstep.

34
00:01:52,683 --> 00:01:54,980
相位的快慢跟着游速走
The phase speeds up with swim speed:

35
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:58,336
加速时尾巴摆得又快又猛，然后滑行
when a fish accelerates its tail beats hard, then it coasts.

36
00:01:59,636 --> 00:02:01,800
咬合很难用正弦波做出来
A bite is hard to make out of sine waves,

37
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,810
于是他们改用混合变形
so they switched to blendshapes:

38
00:02:04,270 --> 00:02:08,104
先张嘴，再把头往前送，同时合上嘴
open the mouth, then thrust the head forward while it snaps shut.

39
00:02:08,864 --> 00:02:11,515
螃蟹的腿也是四个混合姿态
A crab's legs are four blended poses too;

40
00:02:11,515 --> 00:02:15,049
要用骨骼，一只螃蟹就得四十一个关节
with a skeleton, one crab would need forty-one joints.

41
00:02:16,349 --> 00:02:18,562
鱼越长，问题越明显
The longer the fish, the worse it looks:

42
00:02:18,562 --> 00:02:21,697
鲨鱼急转弯时，像一块木板在转
a shark in a hard turn rotates like a plank.

43
00:02:22,257 --> 00:02:24,654
他们给鲨鱼做了四个卷曲姿态
They gave the shark four curl poses,

44
00:02:24,654 --> 00:02:27,201
按转弯的方向和力度在中间插值
blended by the direction and strength of the turn.

45
00:02:27,761 --> 00:02:29,747
可混合变形是叠加的
But blendshapes add up:

46
00:02:29,747 --> 00:02:33,057
向左和向上同时卷，尾巴就被拉得太远
curl left and up at once, and the tail is pulled much too far.

47
00:02:33,717 --> 00:02:37,500
最后只好再加一个专门的斜向姿态，把尾巴拉回来
So they added one more pose just for the diagonal, to pull the tail back.

48
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:42,688
至于每条鱼往哪儿游，就交给上一期的群体规则
Where each fish swims comes from last episode's flocking rules:

49
00:02:42,688 --> 00:02:46,414
位置和速度存在纹理里，在 GPU 上更新
positions and velocities live in textures and update on the GPU.

50
00:02:47,074 --> 00:02:51,176
七种鱼，七次绘制调用，一万零二百四十条鱼
Seven species, seven draw calls, ten thousand two hundred forty fish,

51
00:02:51,176 --> 00:02:53,851
每一条都按自己的节奏在游
each swimming to its own rhythm.

52
00:02:56,151 --> 00:02:58,222
每条鱼，就是一小份数据
Every fish is a tiny bit of data,

53
00:02:58,222 --> 00:03:00,441
加上一段所有鱼共用的代码
plus one piece of code that all fish share.

54
00:03:01,001 --> 00:03:04,115
把这个想法推广到游戏里的每一个对象
Apply that idea to every object in a game,

55
00:03:04,115 --> 00:03:06,451
就是下一期的主角：ECS
and you get the star of the next episode: ECS.

56
00:03:07,351 --> 00:03:11,070
下一期：从《守望先锋》到《僵尸世界大战》
Next time: from Overwatch to World War Z.

57
00:03:11,330 --> 00:03:14,013
而这一切，还得从一条鱼说起
And all of it starts, once again, with a single fish.
